### Running Shell Exercises (`ex00` to `ex05`)

```sh
cd ex03
chmod +x find_sh.sh
./find_sh.sh | cat -e
```

For `ex00`, the submitted `exo.tar` is created from the exercise directory with:

```sh
tar -cf exo.tar *
```

### Compiling Function Exercises (`ex06` to `ex17`, `ex20`, `ex21`, `ex25`, `ex26`)

Function exercises do not contain a `main()`. Compile them together with your own test file and, when needed, with `ft_putchar.c`:

```c
#include <unistd.h>

void	ft_putchar(char c)
{
	write(1, &c, 1);
}
```

Build and run the example:

```sh
cc -Wall -Wextra -Werror ft_putchar.c ex06/ft_print_alphabet.c main.c -o test
./test
```

### Compiling Program Exercises (`ex18`, `ex19`)

```sh
cc -Wall -Wextra -Werror ft_putchar.c ex19/ft_sort_params.c -o a.out
./a.out banana apple cherry
```

### Static Library (`ex24`)

Execute the `Makefile` commands from the exercise directory, which must contain the `srcs/` and `includes/` folders:

| Command       | Description                                                            |
|---------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| `make`        | Compiles the sources in `srcs/` and packages them into `libft.a`       |
| `make clean`  | Removes generated object files (`.o`)                                  |
| `make fclean` | Removes object files (`.o`) and the compiled `libft.a` archive         |
| `make re`     | Cleans all build artifacts (`fclean`) and recompiles from scratch      |

The library only handles the five mandatory functions of this exercise: `ft_putchar`, `ft_putstr`, `ft_strcmp`, `ft_strlen` and `ft_swap`.

### File Display Program (`ex27`)

```sh
cd ex27
make
./ft_display_file file.txt
make fclean
```

| Command       | Description                                                            |
|---------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| `make`        | Compiles the program into the `ft_display_file` binary                 |
| `make clean`  | Removes generated object files (`.o`)                                  |
| `make fclean` | Removes object files (`.o`) and the `ft_display_file` binary           |

Error messages are written to the standard error output, followed by a newline:

| Situation                 | Message                  |
|---------------------------|--------------------------|
| No argument given         | `File name missing.`     |
| More than one argument    | `Too many arguments.`    |
| File cannot be read       | `Cannot read file.`      |

### Norm Check

```sh
norminette ex06 ex07 ex08
```

Shell exercises and the `Makefile` files are not checked by `norminette`.

