| Function                 | Behavior                                                              |
|--------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------|
| `ft_print_alphabet`      | Prints the lowercase alphabet on a single line, starting from `a`     |
| `ft_print_numbers`       | Prints all digits in ascending order on a single line                 |
| `ft_is_negative`         | Prints `N` if `n` is negative, `P` if positive or zero                |
| `ft_ft`                  | Sets the `int` pointed to by `nbr` to `42`                            |
| `ft_swap`                | Swaps the values of two integers through their addresses              |
| `ft_div_mod`             | Stores `a / b` in `*div` and `a % b` in `*mod`                        |
| `ft_iterative_factorial` | Returns the factorial of `nb` using a loop, `0` on error              |
| `ft_recursive_factorial` | Returns the factorial of `nb` using recursion, `0` on error           |
| `ft_sqrt`                | Returns the exact integer square root of `nb`, or `0` if it has none  |

### 3. Strings, Arguments & Memory

| Function          | Behavior                                                                    |
|-------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| `ft_putstr`       | Writes a string to the standard output                                      |
| `ft_strlen`       | Reproduces `strlen`: length of a string excluding the terminating `'\0'`    |
| `ft_strcmp`       | Reproduces `strcmp`: lexicographic comparison of two strings                |
| `ft_print_params` | Program that prints each argument (except `argv[0]`) on its own line        |
| `ft_sort_params`  | Program that prints its arguments in ASCII order, one per line              |
| `ft_strdup`       | Reproduces `strdup`: duplicates a string into newly allocated memory        |
| `ft_range`        | Allocates an `int` array from `min` (included) to `max` (excluded)          |

### 4. Headers & Build System

| Deliverable   | Behavior                                                                      |
|---------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| `ft_abs.h`    | Defines the macro `ABS(Value)` that evaluates to the absolute value           |
| `ft_point.h`  | Defines the `t_point` structure (fields `x` and `y`) used by a given `main`   |
| `Makefile`    | Builds `libft.a` from `srcs/` and `includes/` with `all`, `clean`, `fclean`, `re` |

`ft_point.h` must compile the following code:

```c
#include "ft_point.h"

void	set_point(t_point *point)
{
	point->x = 42;
	point->y = 21;
}

int	main(void)
{
	t_point	point;

	set_point(&point);
	return (0);
}
```

### 5. Advanced Topics

| Function / Program | Behavior                                                                   |
|--------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| `ft_foreach`       | Applies a function `f` to every element of an `int` array, in order        |
| `ft_count_if`      | Counts the strings of a `NULL`-terminated array for which `f` returns `1`  |
| `ft_display_file`  | Prints the content of a file using only `open`, `read`, `write` and `close`|

Prototypes:

```c
void	ft_foreach(int *tab, int length, void (*f)(int));
int		ft_count_if(char **tab, int (*f)(char*));
```

